            {
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "quiz",
              "title": "Allowance or not?",
              "question": "Varun, in the old regime, has no children and has not taken a holiday in three years. HR offers to move ₹72,000 into children education allowance and ₹60,000 into LTA. What happens?",
              "options": [
                "He saves tax on ₹1,32,000",
                "He saves tax on ₹60,000 of LTA only",
                "He saves nothing, both amounts stay taxable unless he qualifies",
                "He loses the money if he does not claim it"
              ],
              "correctIndex": 2,
              "explanation": "Children education allowance is exempt only for actual children, and LTA only against actual domestic travel fare. Without either, both amounts are taxed exactly like special allowance. He does not lose the money, he just gains no exemption. Structuring only works when it matches real spending.",
              "_key": "k58"
